{
  "notes": [
    "Coordinate corrections, applied by db/generate-seed-data.py over the spreadsheet",
    "and by db/schema.sql over the rows already in the database.",
    "",
    "The dataset's coordinates were approximate: many were rounded to 3 decimal places",
    "(about 110 m) and several pins sat on the wrong building, with Dagdusheth's landing",
    "on Tambdi Jogeshwari. Each correction here was matched to a named temple in",
    "OpenStreetMap or Wikidata and then checked by hand. Suggestions that pointed at a",
    "school, a gym or a neighbouring mandal were discarded rather than applied, which is",
    "why this list is short: most pandals are in neither source.",
    "",
    "Each entry records the value it replaces, so it applies only while the source data",
    "still holds that stale value. Fix the spreadsheet and the entry stops doing anything.",
    "",
    "Regenerate candidates with: npm run data:review",
    "",
    "Entries with source \"Google Maps\" (added 2026-09-13) were matched to the named place",
    "on Google Maps. Entries with \"to\": null had no matching named place anywhere, so their",
    "approximate pin is cleared and the site shows the location as unavailable; the Maps",
    "button then searches by name instead of sending visitors to a guessed spot."
  ],
